@startuml
left to right direction

' Build-up for the slides: the step files (sovereignty-deployment-step1.puml
' to -step4.puml) set $STEP and include this file. Every step lays out all
' edges and labels, so the nodes keep their position. Interactions of later
' steps are transparent, those of the current step are green. Without $STEP,
' all interactions show in black.
' Step 0 shows only what the students know before Exercise 9: no pods and
' no interactions (all transparent, so the layout matches the later steps).
' Steps: 1. setup and commission (1-8), 2. bidding and award (9-16),
' 3. award delivery and execution (17-23), 4. result back to the client (24-30).
!$FIRST = 31
!$LAST = 30
!$POD = ""
!if %variable_exists("$STEP")
!if $STEP == 0
!$FIRST = 1
!$LAST = 0
!$POD = "#transparent;line:transparent;text:transparent"
!elseif $STEP == 1
!$FIRST = 1
!$LAST = 8
!elseif $STEP == 2
!$FIRST = 9
!$LAST = 16
!elseif $STEP == 3
!$FIRST = 17
!$LAST = 23
!else
!$FIRST = 24
!$LAST = 30
!endif
!endif

' Label line $t of interaction $n.
!function $l($n, $t)
!if $n > $LAST
!return "<color:transparent>" + $t + "</color>"
!elseif $n >= $FIRST
!return "<color:#00802F>" + $t + "</color>"
!else
!return $t
!endif
!endfunction

' Edge colour for interactions $a < $b < $c on one edge.
!function $e($a, $b = 0, $c = 0)
!if $a > $LAST
!return "#transparent"
!elseif ($a >= $FIRST && $a <= $LAST) || ($b >= $FIRST && $b <= $LAST) || ($c >= $FIRST && $c <= $LAST)
!return "#00802F,thickness=3"
!else
!return "#181818"
!endif
!endfunction

' Minimum deployment for Exercise 9: the sovereignty rules of Task 1 plus the
' pods that Tasks 3 and 4 of the sheet require. Rule 1-3 below are the three
' bullets of Task 1, in order; the sheet does not number them and refers to
' them by name: "task data stays with the client", "worker details stay with
' the worker", "data persistence is moved to pods". Each entity and edge below carries
' a comment that says what in the sheet mandates it, with a link to the line.
' "mandated-by:" marks what the sheet mandates (grep for it); "not mandated"
' marks parts taken from the groups' code (E7/E8).
' Sheet version: Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9 at commit a6cc147.
'
' Rule 2 and Task 4.3 have the worker join a PITAS application, whose auction
' house knows it only by its WebID. As in the groups' code (E7/E8), the Worker
' joins through the worker pool, the auction house only reads the pool, and a won job goes through pitas-jobs and the scheduler to
' the Worker; the auction house never calls the Worker directly.
' The queue carries only notifications with links; the data is in the pods.
' Left out: permission grants, the type index (Task 4.2), and the Auctioneer's
' own worker pool and the Bidder's own auctions (each group plays both roles).
' Timing: only step 11 is placed by a rule. Step 10 could happen at any time
' (the Bidder may keep WebIDs); it comes before step 11 only because the
' WebID is needed to reach the pod.
' Layout: Client and Auctioneer left, Bidder and Worker right, queue and
' auction house pods in between (hidden arrows at the end pin the columns).
' ClientPod and WorkerPod sit under Client and Worker: their own edges use
' -right-> (down in this direction), and [norank] stops 11 and 22/24 from
' pulling them away. Other arrows are written left to right (with <-- for
' the reverse flow); parallel messages share one arrow, numbers give the
' order. Worker setup (1.-3.) comes before the task.

' --- Entities ---------------------------------------------------------------

' Client and ClientPod: mandated-by: Rule 1 stores task input and result in the client's
' pod; Task 1.1 states that the rules require clients to have pods.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L174
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L187
actor Client
database ClientPod $POD

' Auctioneer: mandated-by: the auction house that publishes the auction and reads all bids
' in the integration test.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L241
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L242
node Auctioneer

' EventQueue: not mandated. It is the event plane from Exercise 8; the sheet
' asks whether to keep it next to Solid (Task 5).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L320
queue EventQueue


' AuctionHousePods: grouped to show both as pods of PITAS applications. Not
' mandated: the sheet does not require a shared server; it encourages several.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L162
rectangle AuctionHousePods $POD {
  ' AuctioneerPod: mandated-by: the auction house publishes auctions "in its pod" (Task 3.2)
  ' and has a bid container that only it may read (Task 4.3); Rule 3 moves
  ' persistence to pods, and after a wipe the application rebuilds open
  ' auctions and received bids from pods (Task 3.1).
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L178
  ' Task 1.2 leaves the owner of bids and awards open; this diagram puts them
  ' here because Task 4.3 describes the bid container as the auction house's.
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L241
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L277
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L234
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L188
  database AuctioneerPod $POD

  ' BidderPod: mandated-by: Rule 3 moves persistence to pods; Task 3.1 names
  ' worker IDs as persistent data for pods, and after a wipe the application
  ' rebuilds its registered workers from pods. The registry holds WebIDs only.
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L178
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L232
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L234
  database BidderPod $POD
}



' Bidder: mandated-by: the bidder of the integration test. Its split into components is
' not mandated; it follows the groups' code.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L242
node "PITAS application" as BidderApp {
  node "Bidder" as BidderAH
  ' pitas-worker-pool: not mandated; groups' code. Rule 2 only requires that the
  ' auction house knows the workers of its PITAS application by their WebIDs.
  ' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L176
  node "pitas-worker-pool" as WorkerPool
  ' pitas-jobs + pitas-scheduler: not mandated; groups' code.
  node "pitas-jobs +\npitas-scheduler" as BidderJobs
}

' Worker and WorkerPod: mandated-by: Rule 2 keeps worker details in the worker's pod;
' Task 1.1 states that the rules require workers to have pods.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L176
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L187
control Worker
database WorkerPod $POD

' --- Edges ------------------------------------------------------------------

' 4, 30: mandated-by: Rule 1 stores the input in the client's pod; the commissioning
' client can read the result (Task 3.2).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L174
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L244
Client -[$e(4,30)]right-> ClientPod : $l(4, "4. write task input")\n$l(30, "30. read task result")
' 5: mandated-by: Rule 1 for passing only a link (no intermediary stores
' the input); the commission itself is not mandated.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L174
Client -[$e(5)]-> Auctioneer : $l(5, "5. commission task (link to input)")
' 29: not mandated; groups' code. The link only, as for 5.
Client <-[$e(29)]- Auctioneer : $l(29, "29. notify task done (link to result)")

' 6: mandated-by: the auction house publishes the auction in its pod (Task 3.2), readable
' by anyone (Task 4.3).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L241
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L276
' 14: the auction house can read all bids (Task 3.2, Task 4.3).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L242
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L277
' 16: the auction house awards the auction (Task 3.2); the award is stored in
' a pod (Task 1.3), whose owner Task 1.2 leaves open.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L243
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L189
Auctioneer -[$e(6,14,16)]-> AuctioneerPod : $l(6, "6. create auction (link to input)")\n$l(14, "14. read bids")\n$l(16, "16. write award")
' 7, 17: not mandated; event plane from Exercise 8 (see EventQueue).
Auctioneer -[$e(7,17)]-> EventQueue : $l(7, "7. push auction event (link to auction)")\n$l(17, "17. push award event (link to award)")
' 28: not mandated; event plane from Exercise 8.
Auctioneer <-[$e(28)]- EventQueue : $l(28, "28. deliver result event")
' 15: not mandated; how bids are evaluated is up to the groups.
Auctioneer -[$e(15)]-> Auctioneer : $l(15, "15. evaluate bids")

' 9: mandated-by: the bidder discovers the auction from the auction house's WebID
' (Task 3.2).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L241
' 13: the bidder appends a bid and cannot read others' bids (Task 3.2); the
' bid container is append-only for anyone (Task 4.3).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L242
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L277
' 19: after the award, the task description becomes readable to the winner
' only (Task 3.2, Task 4.3).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L243
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L278
AuctioneerPod <-[$e(9,13,19)]- BidderAH : $l(9, "9. read auction")\n$l(13, "13. append bid (Worker WebID)")\n$l(19, "19. read award")
' 8, 18: not mandated; event plane from Exercise 8.
EventQueue -[$e(8,18)]-> BidderAH : $l(8, "8. deliver auction event")\n$l(18, "18. deliver award event")
' 27: not mandated; event plane from Exercise 8.
EventQueue <-[$e(27)]- BidderAH : $l(27, "27. push result event (link to result)")
' 10: mandated-by: Rule 2 resolves details "starting from the worker's WebID"; when the
' WebIDs are read is not mandated.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L176
BidderAH -[$e(10)]-> WorkerPool : $l(10, "10. fetch registered Worker WebIDs")
' 11: mandated-by: Rule 2 resolves worker details at run time, whenever needed; the bidder
' resolves them "at that moment" (Task 3.2). The read access comes from the
' worker joining the PITAS application (Task 4.3).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L176
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L242
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L280
WorkerPod <-[$e(11),norank]- BidderAH : $l(11, "11. fetch worker details")
' 12: mandated-by: the bidder decides to bid based on its workers' details (Task 3.2).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L242
BidderAH -[$e(12)]-> BidderAH : $l(12, "12. evaluate auction")
' 20, 26: mandated-by: Rule 1 for passing links only (no copies); the
' hand-over and polling themselves are not mandated (groups' code).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L174
BidderAH -[$e(20,26)]-> BidderJobs : $l(20, "20. hand over won job (links only)")\n$l(26, "26. poll job status")

' 1: mandated-by: Rule 2 has the auction house know the worker only by its WebID; joining
' through the worker pool is not mandated (groups' code).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L176
WorkerPool <-[$e(1)]- Worker : $l(1, "1. register (WebID only)")
' 3: mandated-by: Rule 3 and Task 3.1 put worker IDs into pods; the
' application rebuilds its registered workers from them after a wipe.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L178
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L232
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L234
BidderPod <-[$e(3)]- WorkerPool : $l(3, "3. store Worker WebID")
' 2: mandated-by: Rule 2 keeps the worker details in the worker's pod.
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L176
Worker -[$e(2)]right-> WorkerPod : $l(2, "2. write worker details")
' 21, 25: mandated-by: Rule 1 for passing links only (no copies); dispatch
' and report themselves are not mandated (groups' code).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L174
BidderJobs -[$e(21)]-> Worker : $l(21, "21. dispatch (links only)")
BidderJobs <-[$e(25)]- Worker : $l(25, "25. report execution done")
' 22, 24: mandated-by: the worker reads the input from and writes the result into the
' client's pod (Rule 1, Task 3.2); it may write there but read nothing else
' (Task 4.3).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L174
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L244
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L279
ClientPod <-[$e(22,24),norank]- Worker : $l(22, "22. fetch task input")\n$l(24, "24. append task result")
' 23: mandated-by: neither the winner nor any intermediary keeps a copy (Rule 1, Task 3.2).
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L174
' https://github.com/Interactions-HSG/ASSE-Exercise-9/blob/a6cc1472a5d7f5a96cd5a1f38b2769a65e7f8d30/main.tex#L244
Worker -[$e(23)]-> Worker : $l(23, "23. execute (no copy kept)")

' Hidden arrows pin the columns: left apps, queue and pods, Bidder, Worker.
Auctioneer -[hidden]-> AuctionHousePods
Auctioneer -[hidden]-> EventQueue
EventQueue -[hidden]-> BidderApp
AuctionHousePods -[hidden]-> BidderApp

@enduml
